body:
:stop_sign: **Logic Error**: Missing null check before using `hasBackupSecrets` condition. At line 210, `hasBackupSecrets` is assigned based on credential count, but at line 217-223 the code assumes fields exist when creating the Secret. If all r2Fields are undefined (falsy), `providedCount === r2Fields.length` evaluates to true (0 === 5 is false, but 0 === 0 would be true if all are undefined). However, the nullish coalescing operators would then store empty strings. This creates credentials with empty values rather than skipping Secret creation entirely when no credentials are provided.
```suggestion
    const hasBackupSecrets = providedCount === r2Fields.length && providedCount > 0;
    if (hasBackupSecrets) {
      new ApiObject(this, 'r2-credentials-secret', {
        apiVersion: 'v1',
        kind: 'Secret',
        metadata: { name: r2SecretName, namespace, labels: componentLabels(name, 'backup') },
        type: 'Opaque',
        stringData: {
          'r2-account-id': backup.r2AccountId!,
          'r2-bucket': backup.r2BucketName!,
          'r2-access-key-id': backup.r2AccessKeyId!,
          'r2-secret-access-key': backup.r2SecretAccessKey!,
          'restic-password': backup.resticPassword!,
        },
      });
    }
```
